{'review': '{\n  "review": {\n    "overall_status": "NEEDS_FIXES",\n    "quality_score": 7.0,\n    "summary": {\n      "critical": 0,\n      "high": 0,\n      "medium": 2,\n      "low": 2,\n      "passed_checks": [\n        "Type safety",\n        "No hardcoded secrets",\n        "Proper use of useCallback"\n      ]\n    },\n    "findings": [\n      {\n        "finding_id": "F-001",\n        "severity": "medium",\n        "category": "quality",\n        "title": "Race condition in loading state with concurrent requests",\n        "file": "src/hooks/useTodos.ts",\n        "line_range": [\n          15,\n          30\n        ],\n        "description": "The loading state is set to true at the start of each request and false in finally block. If multiple requests overlap (e.g., fetchTodos and getTodo), the first to finish will set loading false while the other is still pending.",\n        "impact": "UI may show loading completed while data is still fetching, leading to inconsistent UI.",\n        "suggested_fix": "Use a loading counter or separate loading flags for different request types, or use a library like react-query that handles request states.",\n        "code_before": "  const fetchTodos = useCallback(async () => {\\n    setLoading(true);\\n    setError(null);\\n    try {\\n      ...\\n    } catch (err: any) {\\n      setError(err.message);\\n    } finally {\\n      setLoading(false);\\n    }\\n  }, [filter]);\\n\\n  const getTodo = useCallback(async (id: string) => {\\n    setLoading(true);\\n    setError(null);\\n    try {\\n      const todo = await getTodoById(id);\\n      return todo;\\n    } catch (err: any) {\\n      setError(err.message);\\n      throw err;\\n    } finally {\\n      setLoading(false);\\n    }\\n  }, []);",\n        "code_after": "  const [loadingCount, setLoadingCount] = useState(0);\\n  const loading = loadingCount > 0;\\n\\n  const fetchTodos = useCallback(async () => {\\n    setLoadingCount(c => c + 1);\\n    setError(null);\\n    try {\\n      let completedFilter: boolean | undefined;\\n      if (filter === \'active\') {\\n        completedFilter = false;\\n      } else if (filter === \'completed\') {\\n        completedFilter = true;\\n      }\\n      const data = await getTodos(completedFilter);\\n      setTodos(data);\\n    } catch (err: any) {\\n      setError(err.message);\\n    } finally {\\n      setLoadingCount(c => Math.max(c - 1, 0));\\n    }\\n  }, [filter]);\\n\\n  const getTodo = useCallback(async (id: string) => {\\n    setLoadingCount(c => c + 1);\\n    setError(null);\\n    try {\\n      const todo = await getTodoById(id);\\n      return todo;\\n    } catch (err: any) {\\n      setError(err.message);\\n      throw err;\\n    } finally {\\n      setLoadingCount(c => Math.max(c - 1, 0));\\n    }\\n  }, []);",\n        "references": []\n      },\n      {\n        "finding_id": "F-002",\n        "severity": "medium",\n        "category": "quality",\n        "title": "Stale data risk due to lack of request cancellation",\n        "file": "src/hooks/useTodos.ts",\n        "line_range": [\n          15,\n          30\n        ],\n        "description": "When filter changes rapidly, earlier getTodos requests may resolve after later ones, causing state to be updated with stale data.",\n        "impact": "UI may display outdated todo list after a quick filter change.",\n        "suggested_fix": "Use an AbortController to cancel previous requests, or ignore responses that are not the latest by tracking a request ID or timestamp.",\n        "code_before": "  const fetchTodos = useCallback(async () => {\\n    setLoading(true);\\n    setError(null);\\n    try {\\n      let completedFilter: boolean | undefined;\\n      if (filter === \'active\') {\\n        completedFilter = false;\\n      } else if (filter === \'completed\') {\\n        completedFilter = true;\\n      }\\n      const data = await getTodos(completedFilter);\\n      setTodos(data);\\n    } catch (err: any) {\\n      setError(err.message);\\n    } finally {\\n      setLoading(false);\\n    }\\n  }, [filter]);",\n        "code_after": "  const fetchTodos = useCallback(async () => {\\n    setLoading(true);\\n    setError(null);\\n    const abortController = new AbortController();\\n    try {\\n      let completedFilter: boolean | undefined;\\n      if (filter === \'active\') {\\n        completedFilter = false;\\n      } else if (filter === \'completed\') {\\n        completedFilter = true;\\n      }\\n      const data = await getTodos(completedFilter, { signal: abortController.signal });\\n      setTodos(data);\\n    } catch (err: any) {\\n      if (err.name !== \'AbortError\') {\\n        setError(err.message);\\n      }\\n    } finally {\\n      setLoading(false);\\n    }\\n    return () => abortController.abort();\\n  }, [filter]);\\n\\n  // Also need to cleanup in useEffect\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    return () => {\\n      // cleanup if needed\\n    };\\n  }, [fetchTodos]);",\n        "references": []\n      },\n      {\n        "finding_id": "F-003",\n        "severity": "low",\n        "category": "quality",\n        "title": "Error handling accesses err.message without type guard",\n        "file": "src/hooks/useTodos.ts",\n        "line_range": [\n          22,\n          24\n        ],\n        "description": "In catch blocks, err is typed as any and err.message is accessed directly. If err is not an Error (e.g., a string), err.message may be undefined, causing error state to be set to undefined (which is not assignable to string | null).",\n        "impact": "Potential runtime TypeError or silent failure where error state becomes undefined, breaking type safety.",\n        "suggested_fix": "Type err as unknown and check if it\'s an Error instance before accessing message, or fallback to a generic message.",\n        "code_before": "    } catch (err: any) {\\n      setError(err.message);\\n    }",\n        "code_after": "    } catch (err) {\\n      let message = \'Unknown error\';\\n      if (err instanceof Error) {\\n        message = err.message;\\n      } else if (typeof err === \'string\') {\\n        message = err;\\n      }\\n      setError(message);\\n    }",\n        "references": []\n      },\n      {\n        "finding_id": "F-004",\n        "severity": "low",\n        "category": "performance",\n        "title": "sortedTodos computed on every render without memoization",\n        "file": "src/hooks/useTodos.ts",\n        "line_range": [\n          70,\n          85\n        ],\n        "description": "The sortedTodos variable is computed each render by spreading and sorting the todos array. While acceptable for small lists, it can be inefficient for larger lists or frequent renders.",\n        "impact": "Unnecessary CPU usage on each render, potentially affecting performance with large todo lists.",\n        "suggested_fix": "Wrap the sorting logic in useMemo, depending on todos, sortBy, and sortOrder.",\n        "code_before": "  const sortedTodos = [...todos].sort((a, b) => {\\n    let compare = 0;\\n    if (sortBy === \'title\') {\\n      compare = a.title.localeCompare(b.title);\\n    } else if (sortBy === \'completed\') {\\n      compare = (a.completed === b.completed) ? 0 : a.completed ? 1 : -1;\\n    }\\n    return sortOrder === \'asc\' ? compare : -compare;\\n  });",\n        "code_after": "  const sortedTodos = useMemo(() => {\\n    return [...todos].sort((a, b) => {\\n      let compare = 0;\\n      if (sortBy === \'title\') {\\n        compare = a.title.localeCompare(b.title);\\n      } else if (sortBy === \'completed\') {\\n        compare = (a.completed === b.completed) ? 0 : a.completed ? 1 : -1;\\n      }\\n      return sortOrder === \'asc\' ? compare : -compare;\\n    });\\n  }, [todos, sortBy, sortOrder]);",\n        "references": []\n      }\n    ],\n    "positive_observations": [\n      "Strong TypeScript usage with explicit types for state and callbacks",\n      "Effective use of useCallback to prevent unnecessary re-renders",\n      "Clear separation of concerns: fetching, adding, updating, deleting todos",\n      "Proper loading and error state management for individual requests",\n      "No hardcoded secrets or sensitive data in the hook"\n    ]\n  }\n}'}